{% comment %}
  Kinsoul Energy — Custom robots.txt
  Preserves Shopify's default crawler rules (checkout, cart, account, etc)
  via robots.default_groups, then adds explicit Allow rules for AI search
  engine crawlers.

  Why each AI crawler is listed:
    GPTBot           — OpenAI training crawler (cite via ChatGPT search)
    ChatGPT-User     — ChatGPT in-conversation browser fetches
    OAI-SearchBot    — OpenAI's search index bot (powers ChatGPT search results)
    ClaudeBot        — Anthropic crawler (cite via Claude with web access)
    anthropic-ai     — Anthropic legacy crawler name (still seen in the wild)
    PerplexityBot    — Perplexity AI search index
    Perplexity-User  — Perplexity in-conversation fetches
    Google-Extended  — Google's AI/Bard training opt-in (separate from googlebot)
    CCBot            — Common Crawl (fuels many open AI training datasets)
    Bytespider       — ByteDance/TikTok search and AI crawler
    Applebot-Extended — Apple Intelligence training crawler

  We explicitly Allow rather than Disallow because we WANT to be cited by
  AI search engines — see llms.txt "Permitted Uses" clause.
{% endcomment -%}

{%- for group in robots.default_groups -%}
  {{- group.user_agent }}
  {%- for rule in group.rules -%}
    {{- rule }}
  {%- endfor -%}
  {%- if group.sitemap != blank -%}
    {{- group.sitemap }}
  {%- endif %}

{% endfor -%}

